doc:article6_issue_1 a echr:Article6Issue ;
    rdfs:label "Alleged violation of Article 6 § 1"@en,
        "applicants' access-to-court grievance"@en,
        "denied access to a court for a determination of their dispute with ESA in connection with an issue under German labour law"@en,
        "violation of Article 6 § 1"@en ;
    echr:affectsParty doc:karlheinzBeer,
        doc:partyApplicants,
        doc:philipRegan ;
    echr:hasIssueDescription "Relying on Article 6 § 1 of the Convention, they complained that they had been denied access to a court for a determination of their dispute with ESA in connection with an issue under German labour law."@en,
        "The applicants contended that they had not had a fair hearing by a tribunal on the question of whether, pursuant to the German Provision of Labour (Temporary Staff) Act, a contractual relationship existed between them and ESA."@en,
        "The applicants maintained that the right of access to the courts was not met merely by institution of proceedings and required that courts examine the merits; they argued that the German courts' application of immunity prevented such examination in their cases."@en,
        "the applicants invited the Court to hold that their rights pursuant to Article 6 § 1 of the Convention had been violated"@en ;
    echr:hasSourceParagraph "33"^^xsd:string,
        "37"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:issueArisesIn doc:domestic_proceeding_1 .

